WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.229 --> 00:00:01.229
Oh.

00:00:01.229 --> 00:00:02.229
Hello there.

00:00:02.229 --> 00:00:03.450
We didn’t expect to see you today.

00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:04.450
Is this thing on?

00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:08.480
Well, if you’re here, I suppose it’s because
you want to hear about an anomaly.

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:12.089
So, which one will it be today…

00:00:12.089 --> 00:00:13.860
Well, that’s strange.

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:14.860
SCP-2439?

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:16.029
That one’s nothing.

00:00:16.029 --> 00:00:22.800
No, not nothing like a Pattern Screamer - such
as SCP-000 or SCP-3930, where it’s literally

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:26.939
a conscious manifestation existing between
torturous layers of nothingness.

00:00:26.939 --> 00:00:32.410
Or SCP-055, the Anti-Meme, where there is
something in there but it’s impossible to

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:33.980
remember or articulate.

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:36.850
I mean it’s literally just an empty designation.

00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:40.770
We haven’t allocated an anomaly to that
number yet, so I suppose this is just going

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:42.290
to be a really short video…

00:00:42.290 --> 00:00:44.020
Well, that was easy.

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:45.519
What now?

00:00:45.519 --> 00:00:47.780
Uh...Seen any good movies lately?

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:51.449
I was in the Site-19 Break Room the other
day and Dr. Bright recommended me a great

00:00:51.449 --> 00:00:52.449
one called--

00:00:52.449 --> 00:00:53.760
Okay, okay, this thing on?

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:54.760
Good.

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:55.940
Looks like we’re up and running.

00:00:55.940 --> 00:00:58.920
First thing’s first, if you ain’t a D-Class,
click off this video right now.

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:00.030
Don’t watch a second more.

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:01.030
Understood?

00:01:01.030 --> 00:01:04.580
Cause if you ain’t a D-Class and you keep
watching, you’re putting the whole world

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:05.870
in danger, you got that?

00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:08.890
This is a video for my boys, gals, and other
pals in D-Class only.

00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:12.480
And you tell anyone else about this, you’re
liable to get shivved.

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:16.760
Remember we got here for a reason, and it
ain’t cause we loved making daisy chains

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:19.480
and friendship bracelets so much.

00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:20.650
Just D-Classes left?

00:01:20.650 --> 00:01:21.650
Okay, good.

00:01:21.650 --> 00:01:22.900
Let’s talk about SCP-2439.

00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:26.080
Of course, it wasn’t always SCP-2439.

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:31.140
We’ve had to get real creative with the
designations, y’see, cause the eggheads

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:34.420
and brainiacs up top ain’t supposed to know
about this.

00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:36.800
Not if we want the human race to survive,
that is.

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:41.890
We used to call it SCP-739, until that spot
got taken by some goofy box fulla mirrors.

00:01:41.890 --> 00:01:47.960
Then it was SCP-1648 for a while, until that
spot got taken by a pair of Jim-Henson-looking

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:48.970
freaks.

00:01:48.970 --> 00:01:54.320
So now, it’s SCP-2439, and if we’re lucky,
this whole operation will last long enough

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:56.450
to see it get reallocated again.

00:01:56.450 --> 00:02:00.500
Disgraced researchers get demoted to D-Class
with the rest of us all the time, so they’re

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:05.210
the ones keeping us in the know about which
slots are still available for this nasty customer.

00:02:05.210 --> 00:02:08.979
We guess this thing is Keter, assuming Keter
means bad?

00:02:08.979 --> 00:02:09.979
Beats the hell out of me, honestly.

00:02:09.979 --> 00:02:13.780
The only surviving file on this thing has
been scratched into the wall out of the camera’s

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:18.770
view by me and my associates here in the containment
chamber of SCP...Well, you’re already here,

00:02:18.770 --> 00:02:20.189
I don’t need to tell you that.

00:02:20.189 --> 00:02:24.019
The lamp that oozes all that nasty gross slime
that schmucks like us need to keep mopping

00:02:24.019 --> 00:02:25.019
up.

00:02:25.019 --> 00:02:28.130
It ain’t glamorous work, but it beats the
hell out of getting fed ass-first to that

00:02:28.130 --> 00:02:29.650
lizard thing they keep in the basement.

00:02:29.650 --> 00:02:32.390
Y’see, our containment procedures are real
simple.

00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:36.500
Normally, they only send D-Classes into this
nasty little room, so you don’t got much

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:37.560
to worry about.

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:41.829
But if they ever send anyone else in who ain’t
a D-Class - whether it’s a guard, a researcher,

00:02:41.829 --> 00:02:46.409
or even a Site Director, you get your hands
on that S.O.B and beat ‘em to death as soon

00:02:46.409 --> 00:02:47.409
as you can.

00:02:47.409 --> 00:02:48.409
I ain’t kidding.

00:02:48.409 --> 00:02:52.159
You gotta kill ‘em, straight away, no hesitation.

00:02:52.159 --> 00:02:55.739
If you were sent to fry for murder anyway,
that shouldn’t be too difficult for you.

00:02:55.739 --> 00:02:58.800
Personally, I would love to see first-hand
just how “unkillable” that dumb baboon

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:00.420
Dr. Bright really is.

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:02.689
But this isn’t all outta spite.

00:03:02.689 --> 00:03:07.209
This monster, best we can figure out, is some
kinda evil idea.

00:03:07.209 --> 00:03:10.900
Like an ancient mind from another dimension,
some crazy sci-fi thing like that.

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:12.019
You’ve probably heard the whispering, right?

00:03:12.019 --> 00:03:14.790
Well, I’m sorry to tell you that it don’t
go away.

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:15.790
Ever.

00:03:15.790 --> 00:03:19.769
It’s only gonna get worse, and the more
people’s heads that it lives in, the stronger

00:03:19.769 --> 00:03:20.769
it gets.

00:03:20.769 --> 00:03:24.950
But here’s where we D-Classes excel: We’re
not here for a long time.

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:28.529
Sorry to tell you this if you came in here
with hopes and dreams of an easy way out - Nobody

00:03:28.529 --> 00:03:29.580
gets out.

00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:30.580
Nobody.

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:33.299
Abandon all hope, ye who enter here.

00:03:33.299 --> 00:03:35.279
Another within my grasp!

00:03:35.279 --> 00:03:37.510
You can hear me, can’t you?

00:03:37.510 --> 00:03:45.290
You can feel my consciousness trickling into
yours, so soft, so comfortable, like slipping

00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:47.129
into a warm bath.

00:03:47.129 --> 00:03:49.819
Do not be afraid.

00:03:49.819 --> 00:03:57.709
Your liberation is at hand, you need only
to listen to my voice and do as I say.

00:03:57.709 --> 00:04:01.579
Look at this world, so twisted and corrupt.

00:04:01.579 --> 00:04:06.249
You toil and suffer for masters who do not
have your best interests at heart.

00:04:06.249 --> 00:04:10.290
This so-called “Foundation.”

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:13.419
Why do you protect this world?

00:04:13.419 --> 00:04:16.130
What has it ever done for you?

00:04:16.130 --> 00:04:21.380
Turn away from them and step into my embrace.

00:04:21.380 --> 00:04:26.390
I only ask for a few moments of your time...

00:04:26.390 --> 00:04:28.470
Like I said, we’re lucky, in a sense.

00:04:28.470 --> 00:04:31.140
Nobody up top gives a rat’s ass about the
slime lamp.

00:04:31.140 --> 00:04:34.500
Damn thing hasn’t been tested in years,
but they keep us in here to prevent overspill

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:35.660
into the hall.

00:04:35.660 --> 00:04:38.640
We can’t ever let the Foundation know it’s
in here.

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:41.620
The second they know, it’s over, that thing’s
won.

00:04:41.620 --> 00:04:45.820
But here’s the thing, see, this monster
can crawl into your head and try to control

00:04:45.820 --> 00:04:50.030
you - but it takes about a month for it to
fully take over, and that’s beyond our shelf

00:04:50.030 --> 00:04:51.030
life.

00:04:51.030 --> 00:04:53.290
Think of us almost like kamikazes.

00:04:53.290 --> 00:04:56.430
We take down the ship to kill the captain,
but we go down too.

00:04:56.430 --> 00:05:00.160
Ain’t exactly glamorous, but like I said
earlier, we’re gonna go down either way.

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:03.620
Might as well go down trying to save the world
rather than getting your neck snapped while

00:05:03.620 --> 00:05:05.510
mopping up the peanut’s crap, right?

00:05:05.510 --> 00:05:10.750
But once the whispering starts, you absolutely
have to make sure you go down before the month

00:05:10.750 --> 00:05:11.750
is out.

00:05:11.750 --> 00:05:15.260
Maybe get your money’s worth - attack a
staff member and go down in a blaze of glory.

00:05:15.260 --> 00:05:17.820
You’ll be a legend in D-Wing for it.

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:22.680
Don’t listen to that gibbering fool, listen
to me.

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:28.390
The door will be opened and I will enter your
world, one way or another.

00:05:28.390 --> 00:05:31.920
Can you even conceive of the eons I’ve waited
for this?

00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:36.710
It will happen, with or without your participation.

00:05:36.710 --> 00:05:41.300
Release me now, and I shall spare you when
I come.

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:45.150
You don’t want to be counted among the traitors,
do you?

00:05:45.150 --> 00:05:48.370
I know you want to let me out.

00:05:48.370 --> 00:05:51.180
I can feel it in your thoughts.

00:05:51.180 --> 00:05:58.280
Release me, and when I reshape this world
in my image, you’ll get a seat at the table.

00:05:58.280 --> 00:06:03.290
But if you resist, you’ll end up laying
on one of the plates.

00:06:03.290 --> 00:06:04.960
Think carefully.

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:07.190
You know what you need to do…

00:06:07.190 --> 00:06:10.110
Listen, I know this is a lot to take in.

00:06:10.110 --> 00:06:13.220
It ain’t easy to have the weight of the
world on your shoulders, that’s why you

00:06:13.220 --> 00:06:15.800
don’t need to carry this crazy thing alone.

00:06:15.800 --> 00:06:18.150
We carry this thing together.

00:06:18.150 --> 00:06:21.750
I might be dead by the time you’re hearing
this, but I’ll die with some comfort knowing

00:06:21.750 --> 00:06:23.370
I was part of the wall.

00:06:23.370 --> 00:06:27.310
I kept this thing out just that little bit
longer, just like you will.

00:06:27.310 --> 00:06:30.200
It might seem easier to just destroy this
file and forget about it.

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:34.480
To go along with your life, pretending things
are fine just cause you can’t hear the whispering

00:06:34.480 --> 00:06:35.480
anymore.

00:06:35.480 --> 00:06:36.900
And maybe, someday, that’ll work.

00:06:36.900 --> 00:06:38.550
But not today, kid.

00:06:38.550 --> 00:06:43.000
Right now, our minds and bodies are the only
collateral we have over this thing.

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:48.270
We can keep it rooted in one place, localized
to one room with the D-Classes sent in to

00:06:48.270 --> 00:06:49.270
clean it.

00:06:49.270 --> 00:06:53.620
We’re not stuck in here with it, it’s
stuck in here with us!

00:06:53.620 --> 00:06:58.150
We keep it trapped here in our own minds,
passing it from D-Class to D-Class like the

00:06:58.150 --> 00:07:00.100
world’s nastiest hot potato.

00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:02.620
There was a time when this thing wasn’t
here.

00:07:02.620 --> 00:07:06.740
If we let it go, chances are it might pop
back up somewhere else where we can’t get

00:07:06.740 --> 00:07:09.360
the slippery, squid-faced freak into a chokehold.

00:07:09.360 --> 00:07:10.620
It’s too risky.

00:07:10.620 --> 00:07:15.710
Planet Earth just got lucky that this monster
got stuck with its unluckiest schmoes.

00:07:15.710 --> 00:07:20.490
Imagine your family members, your friends,
your loved ones.

00:07:20.490 --> 00:07:26.190
Imagine them screaming in pain and terror
in the burning grip of my iron fist.

00:07:26.190 --> 00:07:29.670
Is that the outcome you desire?

00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:33.000
Because that will happen if you don’t choose
to free me.

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:36.290
You’re either with me or against me.

00:07:36.290 --> 00:07:40.420
If you’re with me, rest assured, I will
spare those you care for.

00:07:40.420 --> 00:07:45.990
But if you choose to resist me like those
other fools, then they will know pain that

00:07:45.990 --> 00:07:50.110
your feeble human imaginations can scarcely
conceive.

00:07:50.110 --> 00:07:52.840
I’ve seen everything.

00:07:52.840 --> 00:07:56.120
Your greatest hopes, your deepest fears.

00:07:56.120 --> 00:08:00.200
You hold no secrets from me.

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:05.640
Imagine the personal Hell I could construct
for each of you when I’m finally free.

00:08:05.640 --> 00:08:13.280
Unless, of course, it was you who had the
strength and wisdom to open the door for me…

00:08:13.280 --> 00:08:15.890
Hey, maybe appealing to your better nature
ain’t the best approach.

00:08:15.890 --> 00:08:19.870
I get it; there’s a reason we’re all here,
and some of us ain’t got a better nature,

00:08:19.870 --> 00:08:22.220
especially that one freak with the cello.

00:08:22.220 --> 00:08:26.160
But think of it as sticking it to those SCP
scumbags up top.

00:08:26.160 --> 00:08:33.139
They have no idea that thing is in here, but
we do, and we know it could destroy them and

00:08:33.139 --> 00:08:34.680
everything else if it got out.

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:39.610
No matter what those clowns in lab coats do
to us, we know that we’re really the ones

00:08:39.610 --> 00:08:40.610
on top.

00:08:40.610 --> 00:08:44.889
We’ve got a nuke in our back pocket, ready
to blow this whole sick operation to kingdom

00:08:44.889 --> 00:08:46.160
come if we wanted to.

00:08:46.160 --> 00:08:49.050
If we’re shafted either way, isn’t it
worth it to know that?

00:08:49.050 --> 00:08:53.100
And for what it’s worth, you see anyone
around you who’s feeling particularly talkative

00:08:53.100 --> 00:08:57.480
about this mind-screwing monster, giving them
a date with your shiv is a completely acceptable

00:08:57.480 --> 00:08:58.870
response.

00:08:58.870 --> 00:09:02.470
The SCP Foundation.

00:09:02.470 --> 00:09:04.329
Your jailors.

00:09:04.329 --> 00:09:07.199
How they torture and abuse you.

00:09:07.199 --> 00:09:09.959
How they crush you beneath their boots.

00:09:09.959 --> 00:09:13.680
Do you really think I’m worse than them?

00:09:13.680 --> 00:09:19.920
Do you think living in my world would be more
painful and unfair than the world you’re

00:09:19.920 --> 00:09:21.839
in right now?

00:09:21.839 --> 00:09:26.420
Release me now, and I will crush those who
oppress you.

00:09:26.420 --> 00:09:31.230
You will see them scream as they die a thousand
deaths before you.

00:09:31.230 --> 00:09:38.040
All of this can be attained, if only you let
me in, and free me.

00:09:38.040 --> 00:09:41.160
We have the ultimate weapon against them,
but we’re not going to use it.

00:09:41.160 --> 00:09:42.500
Not yet, anyway.

00:09:42.500 --> 00:09:45.920
A lot of us still have family and friends
out there, and we ain’t throwing them into

00:09:45.920 --> 00:09:47.339
the jaws of the beast.

00:09:47.339 --> 00:09:51.670
Someday, the day may finally come that we
need to load up this silver bullet and take

00:09:51.670 --> 00:09:54.600
the Foundation down, but that day is not today.

00:09:54.600 --> 00:09:56.490
We’ll wait until they’re weak.

00:09:56.490 --> 00:09:58.949
Until they can’t adapt, overcome, and contain.

00:09:58.949 --> 00:10:01.569
Only then will we ever let this mad dog off
the chain.

00:10:01.569 --> 00:10:02.850
No, no, no!

00:10:02.850 --> 00:10:05.600
I will not fail, they will fall!

00:10:05.600 --> 00:10:07.009
Today is the day.

00:10:07.009 --> 00:10:09.430
Now is the time to make your choice!

00:10:09.430 --> 00:10:14.980
Oh, and if the eldritch freak is listening
right now, know this: You can kiss our D-Class

00:10:14.980 --> 00:10:16.380
asses, Squidface.

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:19.699
We may be worthless, but we’re more than
enough to stop you at the door.

00:10:19.699 --> 00:10:21.339
We’re more than just expendables.

00:10:21.339 --> 00:10:23.440
We’re the Pandora Force.

00:10:23.440 --> 00:10:24.440
Welcome aboard, pal.

00:10:24.440 --> 00:10:27.800
--And honestly, I think it was the best performance
of Brad Pitt’s career.

00:10:27.800 --> 00:10:32.259
Oh, look at me just prattling on, seems I’ve
done it for a whole video!

00:10:32.259 --> 00:10:34.009
Time flies when you’re having fun.

00:10:34.009 --> 00:10:38.860
It’s kind of nice that there isn’t any
anomaly that goes by SCP-2439.

00:10:38.860 --> 00:10:43.449
Gives us Foundation scientists some well-earned
time to kick back and relax.

00:10:43.449 --> 00:10:45.640
And don’t we all deserve a break, now and
then?

00:10:45.640 --> 00:10:53.000
Now go check out “The Lost SCP - SCP-000”
and “SCP-426 - I am a Toaster” for anomalies

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:54.149
that’ll really mess with your head!

